# The same two blocks, with the upper one pushed 18 mm out of 20 off the edge.
#
# Nothing about the arrangement itself says this is a problem: it is a perfectly
# good description of where two blocks are, and every static thing PartCAD does
# with it -- rendering it, exporting it, listing what it is made of -- gives the
# same kind of answer it gives for `stable`. What separates the two is what
# happens when the world is switched on, which is what `pc sim` is for: the
# centre of mass of the top block is 8 mm beyond the edge it is resting on, so
# it topples off and ends up on the floor.
links:
  - part: block
    name: bottom
    location: [[0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 1], 0]

  - part: block
    name: top
    location: [[18, 0, 20], [0, 0, 1], 0]
